5. : P2P GO advertises EHT instead of HE
============================================================

ISSUE

P2P GO advertised EHT capabilities even though the expected configuration was HE. This caused an automation failure and was seen as a regression.

TERMS

P2P: Peer-to-Peer. Direct WLAN communication without a traditional AP role.

GO: Group Owner. The AP-like role in a P2P group.

HE: High Efficiency. 802.11ax capability set.

EHT: Extremely High Throughput. 802.11be / Wi-Fi 7 capability set.

WORKAROUND / DEBUG STORY

1. Configured the expected WLAN capability.
2. Used `wl eht features` to verify the EHT configuration.
3. Captured the P2P GO beacon and checked the advertised information elements.
4. Compared the advertised capabilities with the expected HE configuration.
5. Checked the behavior against the previous build.
6. Treated the behavior as a regression and collected the PCAP/capability evidence.

STATUS

The regression was reported with capability evidence. A detailed final RCA or confirmed workaround is not available in the Jira information currently captured.


