12. : Kernel RSN capability regression
============================================================

ISSUE

Association failed after upgrading the Linux kernel from 6.2 to 6.11, even though the same firmware worked with the older kernel.

TERMS

RSN: Robust Security Network.

IE: Information Element. Information carried inside an 802.11 management frame.

cfg80211: Linux wireless configuration framework.

WORKAROUND / DEBUG STORY

1. Captured the Association Request in a sniffer/PCAP.
2. Inspected the RSN Capabilities field.
3. Observed 0x008c instead of the expected 0x0080.
4. Tested the same firmware with kernel 6.2 and 6.11.
5. Used the kernel comparison to isolate the change.
6. Narrowed the issue to cfg80211 RSN IE construction.

STATUS

The kernel-side cfg80211 handling was identified as the regression source. A kernel patch restored successful association.


